      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-61",
        "notes": "Independently checked steps 1.1, 1.2 and 2.1 and every cited supplier statement. Support elimination preserves the represented point and nonnegativity, strictly removes positive indices, and terminates within N reductions, including zero/repeated/dependent generators and empty support. For each nonempty independent support the Gram matrix has trivial kernel, so B=(A^T A)^-1 A^T is a left inverse; Px=x and Bx>=0 characterize exactly its cone. The coordinate/finite triangle estimates give positive violation-ball radii, including identically zero forms; {0} is separately closed. The finitely many support cones have closed union by the finite minimum radius argument. Nonnegative combinations remain in C by coefficient arithmetic. r,N>=1 meet the Euclidean supplier domains; only finite choices occur. Read Kager arXiv:2208.11678v2 pp.1\u20132: its nonzero-matrix convention and sequential proof are context, not imported premises. Reader termination addition is audit enrichment of an already sound finite-descent argument; no finding or unresolved prerequisite."
